  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Energy obligated $52.7B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy recorded 4,776 awards with an average award size of $11M, and obligations were up 8.5% year over year. Obligations rose steadily from $37.7B in FY21 to $52.7B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $41.2B in FY22, $44.6B in FY23, $46B in FY24, and $48.5B in FY25. Facilities Support Services is the largest spending category at $25.3B, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $8.1B and Remediation Services at $3.7B. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is the top vendor at $5.3B, with NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $5.2B and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $3.6B. The page covers contract obligations only, and the FY2026 total is a fiscal year to date figure.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Energy's contract obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy's obligations increased each fiscal year from FY21 through FY26. Obligations moved from $37.7B in FY21 to $41.2B in FY22, $44.6B in FY23, $46B in FY24, $48.5B in FY25, and $52.7B in FY26. The Department of Energy's obligations were up 8.5% year over year for the current fiscal year to date. The FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors account for the largest share of Energy's contracting?",
        "body": "Facilities Support Services accounts for the largest share at $25.3B, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $8.1B and Remediation Services at $3.7B. The Department of Energy's top vendors are TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $5.3B and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $5.2B, with LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $3.6B. Several other vendors exceed $1.6B, including SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC, CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC, and UT-BATTELLE LLC."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Energy spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy obligated $52.7B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy recorded 4,776 awards with an average award size of $11M, and obligations were up 8.5% year over year. The FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Energy buy?",
      "a": "Energy buys a large amount of Facilities Support Services, with $25.3B obligated to that category in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy also obligated $8.1B for Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences and $3.7B for Remediation Services, with additional spending across other R&D and chemical manufacturing categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Energy's largest contractors?",
      "a": "TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is the largest contractor at $5.3B, followed by NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $5.2B and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $3.6B. Other top contractors include SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC ($3.4B), CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC ($3.3B), and UT-BATTELLE LLC ($2.8B)."
